      "lineNbr": 132,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T07:58:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand this is preventing log flooding from an attacker.\nHowever, it is also shielding us from seeing a malicious attempt, if it happens in the 1 minute window.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 132,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "d6c2a10a05c16daf46c01d0848410edb53e194f7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b2c52cd_2817f3ac",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/httpd/RemoteUserUtil.java",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 132,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T09:41:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gerrit error log isn\u0027t a security audit; therefore, we are not really concerned about auditing here, but rather knowing that a request was blocked.\n\nIt\u0027s more serious to run out of disk space because of continuous attacks rather than not knowing all the IPs of the attackers.",
      "parentUuid": "3e052ce0_b767d97c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 132,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "d6c2a10a05c16daf46c01d0848410edb53e194f7",
