    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ceb5c1ff_6e0bfe53",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/pgm/http/jetty/JettyServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 89,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T07:58:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: getRemoteAddress is already documented to be the default, what\u0027s the purpose of setting this explicitly for Jetty?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 89,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 89,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "d6c2a10a05c16daf46c01d0848410edb53e194f7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8dbfe7c_0b263d4c",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/pgm/http/jetty/JettyServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 89,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T08:51:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While `getRemoteAddr()` does return the default TCP peer address initially, calling it here is crucial because of the order of execution.\n\nRight after this line, we call `super.customize(connector, config, request)`, line below.\n\nJetty\u0027s standard `ForwardedRequestCustomizer` will intercept the X-Forwarded-For header and overwrite the remote address on the request object with the client\u0027s original IP.\n\nWe are explicitly saving `request.getRemoteAddr()` into the attribute *before* that happens so that `RemoteUserUtil` can later access the actual, pre-rewrite TCP peer address (the proxy\u0027s IP) to validate it against the trusted CIDR blocks. Without this line, that original proxy IP is lost.\n\nSee also change 595181 for detailed explanation, how it worked before.",
      "parentUuid": "ceb5c1ff_6e0bfe53",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 89,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 89,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "d6c2a10a05c16daf46c01d0848410edb53e194f7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42fd78a2_3977bc81",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/pgm/http/jetty/JettyServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 89,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T09:41:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The default behavior of ForwardedRequestCustomizer is to overwrite the remote address with the value of the `X-Forwarded-For` header, if present. However, it does not \"remember\" the original remote address AFAIK.\n\nSee the original code here below:\n\n```java\n            // Set Remote Address\n            if (forwarded.hasFor())\n            {\n                int forPort \u003d forwarded._for._port \u003e 0 ? forwarded._for._port : request.getRemotePort();\n                request.setRemoteAddr(InetSocketAddress.createUnresolved(forwarded._for._host, forPort));\n            }\n        }\n```\n\nWhat we want to achieve here is to remember what it was the original proxy address *before* calling `super.customize()` and lose access to it.\n\nComment added for making the intent more explicit.",
      "parentUuid": "ceb5c1ff_6e0bfe53",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 89,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 89,
        "endChar": 98
      },
